<PageLayout title="Linux" description="Understand Linux one concept at a time.">
  <h1>Understand your system<span class="dot">.</span></h1>
  <p>Linux is easier to work with when you know what is happening underneath. This is a growing collection of practical explanations.</p>

  <h2>Core concepts</h2>
  <div class="entry">
    <h3>Files and directories</h3>
    <p>Linux organises everything into a filesystem tree. Learn how paths, your home directory, and system directories fit together.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="entry">
    <h3>Permissions</h3>
    <p>Understand read, write and execute permissions, ownership, and what commands like <code>chmod</code> actually change.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="entry">
    <h3>Processes</h3>
    <p>Learn what a running process is, how to inspect it, and how Linux manages programs.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="entry">
    <h3>Packages</h3>
    <p>Understand package managers, repositories, updates, and how software gets installed on your system.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="entry">
    <h3>The terminal</h3>
    <p>Learn commands, arguments, pipes, redirection, and how your shell interprets what you type.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
